{"id":"35e124bc-ad4d-4d06-a80f-e81ea852e37d","revision":0,"last_node_id":17,"last_link_id":35,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"StubeliusLTXTheme","pos":[-960,-120],"size":[480,80],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"theme","name":"theme","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"theme"},"link":null}],"outputs":[],"title":"THEME (this workflow only)","properties":{"aux_id":"stuubszzz/Stubelius-Ultimate-LTX2.5","Node name for S&R":"StubeliusLTXTheme","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["Stuubzzz neon"],"widgets_values_named":{"theme":"Stuubzzz neon"},"color":"#241e2a","bgcolor":"#1b1720"},{"id":2,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-1580,-120],"size":[600,1760],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"HOW TO USE","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"MarkdownNote","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["# Ultimate LTX — how to use\n\nWork top to bottom: **Setup → Seed Samplers → Models → Output → Director → Seeds → Finish**. Everything is chosen up front; after a seed hunt only **WINNER** is left.\n\n## 1 · SETUP and SEED SAMPLERS — how the seeds are rendered\n- **seeds** — how many full videos (with sound) to render, 1–4.\n- **seed** — seed 1; seeds 2–4 add 1000003 each. Keep its **control after generate on fixed**, or the finish re-renders new seeds.\n- **steps / cfg** — 8 steps, cfg 1: the official distilled first pass.\n- **first pass scale** — **1.0 (default): the seeds render at full size** and the winner is finished as rendered, with real HD detail. Below 1 (e.g. 0.5) = quicker, softer seeds: Finish then upscales the winner x2 in latent space and refines it, which can't add the detail a half-size render never had.\n- **SEED SAMPLERS** — a sampler and scheduler for each seed; the slots past **seeds** are greyed out and not used. euler_ancestral + linear_quadratic is the official first pass (linear_quadratic at 8 steps is exactly Lightricks' distilled sigmas); give another seed euler or another sampler for variety.\n- Changing anything here **re-renders** the seeds.\n\n## 2 · MODELS — what it runs on\n- **diffusion model** — the LTX 2.5 checkpoint (safetensors or GGUF). A non-distilled checkpoint needs the **distill LoRA** (8 steps, cfg 1); the Stubelius remix has it baked in.\n- **extra LoRA 1–2** — apply to the seeds and the refine. **IC-LoRA** — for the Director's motion / video guides.\n- **MSR LoRA** — its own slot (Licon **LTX-2.5-Licon-MSR-V2**, V1 also works), used in both passes when the Director's reference option is **Licon MSR**, ignored otherwise. **msr lora strength** is the first pass (the seeds); the refine's is on Output.\n- **text encoder, video / audio VAE, latent upscaler** — LTX 2.5 files (2.5 needs the Gemma 4 encoder).\n- **attention** — **sage attention** (KJNodes), **comfy kitchen attention** (ComfyUI's own quantized INT8 attention, Nvidia / AMD) or **comfyui default** (whatever ComfyUI was started with). One at a time: they replace each other.\n- **speed & memory** — memory-efficient attention (its own Sage kernel for the self-attention, whichever attention is picked) and chunked feed-forward use less VRAM. **decode tile size** — the largest spatial tile; each clip is decoded in one temporal pass (no flicker between chunks). When a clip doesn't fit in the free VRAM at this tile, the decode steps it down by itself instead of spilling into system RAM.\n- **live preview** — tiny LTX VAE for the **LIVE PREVIEW** panel; off = ComfyUI's default preview on the sampling node.\n\n## 3 · OUTPUT — what comes out (set it now, change it any time)\n- **refine strength / steps / sampler** — only when first pass scale is below 1: the winner is upscaled x2 in latent space and refined at full size from this noise level. 0.3–0.45 keeps the seed's look; higher (the official template restarts at 0.85–0.91) changes the look but adds little detail. euler = no new noise in the refine, as Lightricks' pipeline.\n- **refine MSR LoRA strength / refine MSR reference** — also only below full size; the second pass of MSR: the LoRA's strength in the refine, and how hard the reference images pull there. ~0.4 keeps the detail without the references repainting the opening (no second-pass mist or ghosting); 0 = the Director's reference strength, which the seeds always use.\n- **audio** — keep the seed's sound exactly as you heard it, or let the refine regenerate it.\n- **final resolution** — native (the Director's size) or 720p–4K; the short side lands exactly on the number, portrait too. 4K holds ≈100 MB of RAM per frame: keep 4K clips short, especially at 48–60 fps.\n- **final fps** — 0 = the Director's frame rate, untouched; 48 / 50 / 60 via RIFE, length and sync kept, hard cuts stay clean.\n- **upscaler** — RTX VSR, or DLSS5 + Color Lock (more detail, original colours).\n- Output feeds only Finish, so changing it **never re-renders** the seeds.\n\n## 4 · DIRECTOR — what the video is\nThe timeline: prompts, images (first frame, last frame, keyframes), audio and motion tracks, size, frame rate and duration. The reference option **Licon MSR** (character and ingredient images) needs the **MSR LoRA** on Models; its reference strength drives the seeds.\n\n## 5 · SEEDS and FINISH — pick the winner\n**winner** — which seed to finish; **0 = hold** after the seeds. That's the only choice left after a seed hunt.\n\n**Seed hunt:** set seeds = 3 and **winner = 0** (hold) and queue → watch Seed 1–3 → set winner 1–3 on Finish → queue again (only the finish runs; the seeds come from cache). Winner 1+ on the first run finishes that seed straight away. Don't touch Setup / Seed Samplers / Models / Director in between.\n"],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"# Ultimate LTX — how to use\n\nWork top to bottom: **Setup → Seed Samplers → Models → Output → Director → Seeds → Finish**. Everything is chosen up front; after a seed hunt only **WINNER** is left.\n\n#